WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.250
I couldn't be more excited to help kick beauty week off

2
00:00:04.250 --> 00:00:07.960
with this extraordinary young woman.

3
00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:11.660
I actually found an article about her many months ago,

4
00:00:11.660 --> 00:00:14.720
and I said to the team, "Could we have her on the show?"

5
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:17.350
And she's here, so it's happening.

6
00:00:17.350 --> 00:00:20.870
And 16 years old,

7
00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:24.390
she's the youngest black beauty store owner in the country.

8
00:00:24.390 --> 00:00:25.603
Please, take a look.

9
00:00:26.930 --> 00:00:28.560 line:15%
Hi, I'm Paris McKenzie.

10
00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.900 line:15%
I'm 16 years old.

11
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:32.560 line:15%
And I'm the proud owner of Paris Beauty Supplyz

12
00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:33.650 line:15%
in Brooklyn, New York.

13
00:00:33.650 --> 00:00:37.150 line:15%
Both of my parents immigrated from Spanish Town, Jamaica,

14
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:41.200
and I'm one of our first-generation children in this country

15
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:42.740
to be a citizen.

16
00:00:42.740 --> 00:00:45.920
Without their hard work and without their determination,

17
00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:48.460
we wouldn't be as successful as we are now.

18
00:00:48.460 --> 00:00:52.000
We came from not sleeping on any furniture

19
00:00:52.000 --> 00:00:54.230
to owning our own home.

20
00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:57.970
All my life, I've been working in stores owned by my mother.

21
00:00:57.970 --> 00:01:00.700 line:15%
About one to two years ago,

22
00:01:00.700 --> 00:01:03.530 line:15%
I started working more independently in the salon.

23
00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.690 line:15%
So, I started taking clients and I did hair and I did nails.

24
00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:10.000
And on a school day, I will go to high school,

25
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.520
I go to college, and then I'll come straight to work after.

26
00:01:13.520 --> 00:01:16.293
One day, the previous owners of the Beauty Supplyz store

27
00:01:16.293 --> 00:01:19.930
came to my mom and told her that they were selling.

28
00:01:19.930 --> 00:01:22.780
So, she came to me and asked me if I wanted to invest,

29
00:01:22.780 --> 00:01:24.520
and I said, "Yes, of course."

30
00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:29.020
To be able to do this and take a huge step in my life goal

31
00:01:29.020 --> 00:01:30.920
was something I couldn't pass up.

32
00:01:30.920 --> 00:01:32.790
I had to mature very quickly.

33
00:01:32.790 --> 00:01:35.280
I had to learn how to handle money,

34
00:01:35.280 --> 00:01:38.540
how to handle business at a very, very young age.

35
00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:41.650 line:15%
There are so many people that are in young people's ears

36
00:01:41.650 --> 00:01:43.210 line:15%
like, "You can't do it yet."

37
00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:46.440 line:15%
So, seeing my story should help them erase

38
00:01:46.440 --> 00:01:48.220 line:15%
all of those negative thoughts

39
00:01:48.220 --> 00:01:50.330
so they can go and try to achieve

40
00:01:50.330 --> 00:01:51.740
whatever they want to in life.

41
00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:55.620
I just wanna be able to give them the opportunity

42
00:01:55.620 --> 00:01:59.013
to build up that courage and give them that motivation.

43
00:01:59.013 --> 00:02:00.730
(audience applauds)

44
00:02:00.730 --> 00:02:05.390
Okay, I was redoing my homework on you last night,

45
00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:08.700
and I was reading this L article that you did.

46
00:02:08.700 --> 00:02:13.040
First of all, Bella Hadid and Janet Jackson

47
00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.090
was Tweeting and Instagramming about your story.

48
00:02:17.090 --> 00:02:19.870
And one of the things I loved in the article

49
00:02:19.870 --> 00:02:24.850
was that you said you have a very amazing prowess

50
00:02:24.850 --> 00:02:27.910
for salesmanship and identifying what a customer...

51
00:02:27.910 --> 00:02:28.743
When they come and you say,

52
00:02:28.743 --> 00:02:31.930
"I clock their style, kind of who they are.

53
00:02:31.930 --> 00:02:35.400
And I think intuitively, I know maybe what they need."

54
00:02:35.400 --> 00:02:38.150
And that you yourself, when you would walk through stores,

55
00:02:38.150 --> 00:02:40.770
did not only not get assistance,

56
00:02:40.770 --> 00:02:43.420
but not really any help at all.

57
00:02:43.420 --> 00:02:44.990
In fact, a bit of the opposite.

58
00:02:44.990 --> 00:02:49.990
So, what about your experience made you be so proactive?

59
00:02:52.620 --> 00:02:56.340
Well, when I was in beauty supply stores

60
00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:58.210
and when I would walk in,

61
00:02:58.210 --> 00:03:01.810 line:15%
I wouldn't get the experience I felt like I needed.

62
00:03:01.810 --> 00:03:04.390 line:15%
Being black and having natural hair

63
00:03:04.390 --> 00:03:08.230 line:15%
and being young as well, not really knowing your identity,

64
00:03:08.230 --> 00:03:12.150
you kind of want someone to help you be guided on your path.

65
00:03:12.150 --> 00:03:13.840
And I never got that experience.

66
00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:15.880
So, being the person that I am,

67
00:03:15.880 --> 00:03:18.990
I wouldn't want other people to feel the same way I did.

68
00:03:18.990 --> 00:03:21.920
So I thought, "Let me use this store

69
00:03:21.920 --> 00:03:26.070
as a way to empower other women or any gender

70
00:03:26.070 --> 00:03:29.600
and empower people who don't get that experience

71
00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:31.700
so they can love themselves

72
00:03:31.700 --> 00:03:34.163
and make themselves more beautiful.

73
00:03:35.440 --> 00:03:37.200
You're 16?

74
00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:39.560
Yes. (chuckles)
Paris, what is going on?

75
00:03:39.560 --> 00:03:42.980
You act and look so mature.

76
00:03:42.980 --> 00:03:46.110
You're balancing homework and college

77
00:03:46.110 --> 00:03:48.030
and running a business.

78
00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:51.280
How do you think that you became...

79
00:03:51.280 --> 00:03:52.830
I started young too,

80
00:03:52.830 --> 00:03:54.870
and I don't even have anything to pull from.

81
00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:58.160
I'm just staring at you and, oh, how do you do what you do?

82
00:03:58.160 --> 00:04:00.540
Well, I have a schedule set now,

83
00:04:00.540 --> 00:04:03.060 line:15%
and I go to high school in the mornings,

84
00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:05.610 line:15%
and I go to college in the afternoons,

85
00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:07.170 line:15%
but it's only two days a week.

86
00:04:07.170 --> 00:04:09.870 line:15%
And then I'm in the store the whole day

87
00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:11.520
until after eight o'clock.

88
00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.930
And then at night, I go back to high school work.

89
00:04:14.930 --> 00:04:16.640
And that's the schedule I have,

90
00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.600
but really, the work ethic I got

91
00:04:18.600 --> 00:04:20.600
was from watching my mother.

92
00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.280
She's a entrepreneur herself,

93
00:04:22.280 --> 00:04:24.680
and she owns two businesses as well.

94
00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:27.880
And just watching her and growing up around her

95
00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:31.980
is what really what taught me to be what I am now

96
00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:35.750
and how to have that work ethic and that determination.

97
00:04:35.750 --> 00:04:37.520
Well, as a mother of two daughters,

98
00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:42.040
I can only marvel at your and your mother's grace.

99
00:04:42.040 --> 00:04:43.760
It's just so inspiring.

100
00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:48.690
And it's so just dope and awesome and cool and inspiring,

101
00:04:48.690 --> 00:04:51.710
as well as really elegantly pointed

102
00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:55.500
in business, organization, prioritizing.

103
00:04:55.500 --> 00:04:57.810
I wanna introduce you to a trailblazer

104
00:04:57.810 --> 00:04:59.030
in this beauty industry.

105
00:04:59.030 --> 00:05:01.480
And after working with makeup for over a decade

106
00:05:01.480 --> 00:05:03.620
and feeling like there was still a void

107
00:05:03.620 --> 00:05:04.990
in options for black women,

108
00:05:04.990 --> 00:05:06.660
she took matters into her own hand

109
00:05:06.660 --> 00:05:09.000
and created this company, UOMA.

110
00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.010
And it's Sharon Chuter, who's here.

111
00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:14.131
Sharon, hello.

112
00:05:14.131 --> 00:05:17.300
Hi, hi guys from Los Angeles. (laughs)

113
00:05:17.300 --> 00:05:19.670
Sharon, I have so much to talk to you about today,

114
00:05:19.670 --> 00:05:22.310
but with Paris, I mean, when you hear her story,

115
00:05:22.310 --> 00:05:24.900
does it feel reminiscent of your own?

116
00:05:24.900 --> 00:05:28.440
Is there parallels? What are your thoughts?

117
00:05:28.440 --> 00:05:30.500
Oh my God, firstly, I'm blown away.

118
00:05:30.500 --> 00:05:32.660
Paris, you are amazing.

119
00:05:32.660 --> 00:05:35.690
I am a super fan. I love what you're doing.

120
00:05:35.690 --> 00:05:37.500
And yes, there is so much parallels

121
00:05:37.500 --> 00:05:40.810 line:15%
because a lot of people don't know this about my story,

122
00:05:40.810 --> 00:05:42.680 line:15%
but I actually brought Revlon into Nigeria

123
00:05:42.680 --> 00:05:43.940 line:15%
when I was a teenager.

124
00:05:43.940 --> 00:05:46.310 line:15%
So, my story is very similar to yours,

125
00:05:46.310 --> 00:05:48.470
really starting that entrepreneurial path

126
00:05:48.470 --> 00:05:49.410
while I was really young.

127
00:05:49.410 --> 00:05:50.860
I mean, I wasn't as young as you,

128
00:05:50.860 --> 00:05:52.930
I was only a couple of years older than you were

129
00:05:52.930 --> 00:05:55.690
at the time that I did that, so I am amazed,

130
00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:58.530
I'm in awe, and I could not be proud of what you do

131
00:05:58.530 --> 00:05:59.910
right now (indistinct).

132
00:05:59.910 --> 00:06:03.900
And your store, Paris, is so extraordinary.

133
00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:06.120
I've looked at the shelves and the stocking

134
00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:09.300
and your curation and your knowledge of the products.

135
00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.950
And Sharon, we're gonna talk in the next segment

136
00:06:11.950 --> 00:06:14.840
about all the pioneering you've done.

137
00:06:14.840 --> 00:06:19.090
And I believe you have something for Paris.

138
00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:21.280
Yes, I do, Paris.

139
00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:24.230
So, I am such a fan of what you're doing,

140
00:06:24.230 --> 00:06:26.990
and I would love to support you in any way I can.

141
00:06:26.990 --> 00:06:29.680
And there's two ways that I would love to support you.

142
00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:32.240
First part is your education because it's so important.

143
00:06:32.240 --> 00:06:35.770
Very similar to you, I did start an entrepreneurial path,

144
00:06:35.770 --> 00:06:37.890
but I did go back and continue working

145
00:06:37.890 --> 00:06:38.850
and continue studying.

146
00:06:38.850 --> 00:06:41.980
So, I would love to contribute $5,000

147
00:06:41.980 --> 00:06:44.416
towards your education to make sure

148
00:06:44.416 --> 00:06:45.734
that you continue-
Oh my God!

149
00:06:45.734 --> 00:06:47.480
because it is super important.

150
00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:49.520
Oh my God!
And the second thing

151
00:06:49.520 --> 00:06:52.247
I would love to do is also give you

152
00:06:52.247 --> 00:06:56.120
$5,000 worth of products as well from UOMA Beauty,

153
00:06:56.120 --> 00:06:58.450
so that you can display them proudly.

154
00:06:58.450 --> 00:06:59.870
And I hope in doing that,

155
00:06:59.870 --> 00:07:02.770
you get even more beauty brands support you

156
00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.970
and come on board on your shelves, but I am beyond proud.

157
00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.480
Well done.

158
00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:10.110
Thank you. Thank you so much.

159
00:07:10.110 --> 00:07:11.210
Thank you so much.
Paris,

160
00:07:11.210 --> 00:07:14.030
you really are the shining example.

161
00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:16.490
I mean, you just have blown me away

162
00:07:16.490 --> 00:07:18.810
since I found out about your story several months ago.

163
00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:22.520
I am so honored to be on a show with you.

164
00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:24.850
Work with Sharon, shine a light.

165
00:07:24.850 --> 00:07:27.370
I'm really impressed with you.

166
00:07:27.370 --> 00:07:29.890
And I think you have so many things

167
00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:31.690
in your brightest of future

168
00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:34.820
and so many people to carry and lift up with you

169
00:07:34.820 --> 00:07:36.780
because you've clearly figured out

170
00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:38.280
a way to pull this all off.

171
00:07:38.280 --> 00:07:39.760
So, thank you, Paris.

172
00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:42.210
Sharon, we'll be back in a minute to talk more with you

173
00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:43.470
right after the break.

174
00:07:43.470 --> 00:07:44.539
Thank you, Paris.

175
00:07:44.539 --> 00:07:47.122 line:15%
(upbeat music)

